{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 125, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the direct input-output shortcut where none exists gives large gains (exps 7, 11, 12), unlike replacing an existing conv, pool or 1x1 op on that edge (exps 8-10)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the edge-3 shortcut, a skip on edge 0 restores a residual-like path (exp 44: +15 on IN16) instead of just weakening a conv (exp 38)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Skip on edge 4 helps on all three datasets when edge 3 is missing (exp 47) but hurts when the shortcut exists (exp 41)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Skip on edge 5 restores a short path to the output when edge 3 is none (exp 48 positive), whereas with edge 3 present it is mostly harmful (exp 42)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Converting edge 0 to a conv from skip in a conv-free cell yields huge gains (exp 77), far more than replacing a 1x1 conv (exp 83) or none in a conv-rich cell (exp 95)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing parameter-free pooling with a 3x3 conv adds learnable capacity (exps 72, 98), giving more than replacing none or a 1x1 conv (exps 54-57, 84)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "When the rest of the cell is pooling, the edge-3 conv is the only parametric path, so its gain is much larger (exps 60, 74) than in conv-rich parents (exps 58, 89)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "In skip-dominated cells, adding a conv on the final edge supplies missing capacity (exps 6, 82), unlike conv-heavy parents where it gives mixed results (exps 1-5)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 also absent, removing edge 0 cuts the input off from nodes 1 and 2 and collapses the network (exp 17), unlike the mild effects seen otherwise (exps 13-16)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the identity shortcut from input to output is far more damaging than deleting a conv on that edge (exps 69, 90), consistent with how much adding that skip helps (exps 7, 11, 12)."}], "tok": 17416, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["none", "nor_